Kind: widen
Issue: #687
Holds open: an aborted RPC's window between its reply being written and the wakeup that comes with it -- a thread the hot path parked, let go by an abort, comes back for its reply 100 ms late, so that a reply sent after the abort finds it still queued, and the reply's deliverer, finding its receiver already out of its wait, holds the wakeup 300 ms; each side says so, so that a fixed arm that passes shows the window was open; in the fixed tree the receiver waits for that wakeup under imq_lock; the deliverer says when its wakeup is about to end a later wait; only the first 16 of each in a boot, since act_test [11] aborts a thread some 2000 times
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_mqueue.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_mqueue.c
